WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.319
(airplane sound)

00:00:03.319 --> 00:00:04.152
- [Evan] What's up Believe Nation?

00:00:04.152 --> 00:00:06.177
It's Evan, my one word is believe

00:00:06.177 --> 00:00:07.559
and I believe in people

00:00:07.559 --> 00:00:09.373
more than they believe in themselves,

00:00:09.373 --> 00:00:12.614
and my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:12.614 --> 00:00:16.330
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.419
I started the Believe Life Series

00:00:17.419 --> 00:00:19.829
to help us learn a little
bit more about ourselves,

00:00:19.829 --> 00:00:21.077
grow personally,

00:00:21.077 --> 00:00:24.233
and ideally bring some of
what we learn about ourselves,

00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:26.354
to our business to have more success.

00:00:26.354 --> 00:00:30.180
So today we're going to learn
how to be optimistic in life.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.763
(upbeat music)

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:47.680
(whimsical music)

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.286
- [Gary] I think the
biggest obstacle to success

00:00:51.286 --> 00:00:53.119
is a lack of optimism.

00:00:54.369 --> 00:00:57.007
I think the world like lacks optimism.

00:00:57.007 --> 00:00:59.286
I think, you know, everyone's like,

00:00:59.286 --> 00:01:00.719
"Your energy, your energy."

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:03.185
I've come to realize, it's just optimism,

00:01:03.185 --> 00:01:05.352
just happy, just positive.

00:01:06.236 --> 00:01:08.067
That's what it is.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.900
(whimsical music)

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:12.689
- [Tony] Most of us have situations

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:14.751
where there are, for all of you listening,

00:01:14.751 --> 00:01:17.290
a place where you have
some unfinished business.

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.265
(laughter)

00:01:18.265 --> 00:01:20.826
- [Tim] That's the story
of my life, Tony. (laughs)

00:01:20.826 --> 00:01:22.618
- [Tony] Okay well I do a
story of all our lives, right?

00:01:22.618 --> 00:01:24.572
That's just being human, right?

00:01:24.572 --> 00:01:26.844
But it's a place where
there's something that

00:01:26.844 --> 00:01:28.613
you should have handled,
and you haven't handled,

00:01:28.613 --> 00:01:30.181
with a person or situation,

00:01:30.181 --> 00:01:31.596
it stresses you out.

00:01:31.596 --> 00:01:33.520
And so what we tend to do
is focus on other stuff

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.954
'cuz we don't want to
have to deal with that

00:01:34.954 --> 00:01:37.762
'cuz it's stressful, 'cuz
it's, you know, painful.

00:01:37.762 --> 00:01:40.480
And so think of something
that on a zero to ten scale,

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.120
where ten is totally stressed
out and zero is not at all,

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.057
pick something that's unfinished business

00:01:45.057 --> 00:01:46.744
in your business or personal life,

00:01:46.744 --> 00:01:47.859
with something or someone,

00:01:47.859 --> 00:01:50.223
and it's at least a seven,
eight, nine, or a ten.

00:01:50.223 --> 00:01:52.255
Just so you can see
that this really works.

00:01:52.255 --> 00:01:53.542
Now by the way, there are
hundreds of ways to do this.

00:01:53.542 --> 00:01:54.847
I'm just going to give you this one,

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.597
'cuz we can do it in two minutes, alright.

00:01:56.597 --> 00:01:59.920
So, I'm hoping, Tim do
you have one by chance?

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:00.753
- [Tim] I do.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.867
- [Tony] Okay perfect.

00:02:01.867 --> 00:02:03.834
Give me the topic of content,
no one else tells the content.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.150
Alright. Everyone if you
would, just for a moment,

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:06.658
and I don't have any
music in the background

00:02:06.658 --> 00:02:07.919
which I need to enhance this normally,

00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:08.752
but let's just do it.

00:02:08.752 --> 00:02:10.916
Put both your hands on your heart,

00:02:10.916 --> 00:02:14.583
and physically breathe
deep into your heart.

00:02:16.399 --> 00:02:19.176
And as you're breathing
deep in your heart,

00:02:19.176 --> 00:02:21.991
feel the strength of you heart.

00:02:21.991 --> 00:02:24.408
Feel the power of your heart.

00:02:27.017 --> 00:02:29.517
Feel the beauty of your heart.

00:02:30.811 --> 00:02:33.478
What are you proud, or grateful,

00:02:34.663 --> 00:02:37.311
that your heart has guided you to do?

00:02:37.311 --> 00:02:38.228
Or to give?

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.898
Or to feel?

00:02:40.898 --> 00:02:41.898
Or to enjoy?

00:02:44.488 --> 00:02:46.016
And feel of the strength of your heart,

00:02:46.016 --> 00:02:47.043
breathe into it.

00:02:47.043 --> 00:02:49.710
Feel the blood flow, the oxygen.

00:02:50.761 --> 00:02:53.849
And feel grateful for your heart first.

00:02:53.849 --> 00:02:55.199
Just think about it,

00:02:55.199 --> 00:02:57.387
you didn't have to earn this heart,

00:02:57.387 --> 00:02:59.690
it was given to you.

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.697
You didn't have to prove
your value or your worth,

00:03:01.697 --> 00:03:04.120
you didn't have to accomplish anything.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.042
Something loved you enough
to give you the gift of life.

00:03:07.042 --> 00:03:09.020
As long as this heart is beating,

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.046
you have that gift,

00:03:10.046 --> 00:03:11.717
and you live.

00:03:11.717 --> 00:03:13.846
It beats 100,000 times a day.

00:03:13.846 --> 00:03:16.574
It pumps blood through 60,000
miles of blood vessels,

00:03:16.574 --> 00:03:17.639
they put 'em end to end,

00:03:17.639 --> 00:03:19.512
they go around the world
twice at the equator.

00:03:19.512 --> 00:03:21.412
That's what's inside every one of us.

00:03:21.412 --> 00:03:24.880
And you don't have to think
about it, what a gift.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:25.995
So as you breathe in your heart,

00:03:25.995 --> 00:03:28.991
feeling your powerful heart,

00:03:28.991 --> 00:03:29.941
I want you just for a moment,

00:03:29.941 --> 00:03:31.213
we're going to think of three,

00:03:31.213 --> 00:03:33.152
but just think first of
one event in your life,

00:03:33.152 --> 00:03:35.728
one experience, one moment,

00:03:35.728 --> 00:03:39.649
that you could feel so
grateful for if you wanted to,

00:03:39.649 --> 00:03:42.316
a magic moment, a sacred moment,

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:45.262
a sexy moment, a beautiful
moment, a loving moment,

00:03:45.262 --> 00:03:48.622
any moment that really you
could feel grateful for,

00:03:48.622 --> 00:03:49.921
if you wanted to right now.

00:03:49.921 --> 00:03:51.997
And then step into that
memory for a minute,

00:03:51.997 --> 00:03:55.663
like step in your body
as if you were there.

00:03:55.663 --> 00:03:57.545
See what you would have saw,

00:03:57.545 --> 00:03:58.885
as if you're there.

00:03:58.885 --> 00:04:01.643
Or hear what you'd hear, back then.

00:04:01.643 --> 00:04:05.087
Breathe the way you were
breathing back then.

00:04:05.087 --> 00:04:07.554
And if you fill up with
that sense of gratitude

00:04:07.554 --> 00:04:09.219
for that moment,

00:04:09.219 --> 00:04:13.386
how do you smile when you feel
so grateful or so thankful?

00:04:14.918 --> 00:04:16.538
What's the look in your eyes?

00:04:16.538 --> 00:04:17.742
How do you breathe?

00:04:17.742 --> 00:04:19.147
Let's look in your face

00:04:19.147 --> 00:04:22.230
when you feel really really grateful.

00:04:23.305 --> 00:04:25.446
And just fill it up,
fill up with gratitude.

00:04:25.446 --> 00:04:28.515
The reason we use gratitude, by the way,

00:04:28.515 --> 00:04:32.808
the two emotions that mess
us up most is anger and fear.

00:04:32.808 --> 00:04:35.696
And you can't be grateful
and angry simultaneously,

00:04:35.696 --> 00:04:37.768
it's the antidote.

00:04:37.768 --> 00:04:40.599
You can't be fearful and
angry simultaneously.

00:04:40.599 --> 00:04:41.951
So fill up with gratitude,

00:04:41.951 --> 00:04:43.262
now think of a second moment

00:04:43.262 --> 00:04:44.532
you can feel truly grateful for,

00:04:44.532 --> 00:04:47.513
and again breathe deep in your heart,

00:04:47.513 --> 00:04:48.846
feel that power.

00:04:49.888 --> 00:04:50.721
Just think of any other moment,

00:04:50.721 --> 00:04:52.754
it could be from your
childhood or adulthood.

00:04:52.754 --> 00:04:54.087
It could be last week, it could be today,

00:04:54.087 --> 00:04:55.215
it could be ten years ago.

00:04:55.215 --> 00:04:57.848
Any moment that you can
just truly feel like

00:04:57.848 --> 00:05:01.412
that was the greatest, that was
magical, that was beautiful,

00:05:01.412 --> 00:05:03.125
that's magnificent.

00:05:03.125 --> 00:05:04.096
Something that gives you the feeling

00:05:04.096 --> 00:05:05.481
of tremendous gratitude,

00:05:05.481 --> 00:05:08.566
if you really focused on it.

00:05:08.566 --> 00:05:10.233
Breathe it, feel it,

00:05:11.325 --> 00:05:12.158
enjoy it.

00:05:13.317 --> 00:05:15.234
Fill up with gratitude.

00:05:17.199 --> 00:05:18.824
Then finally, think of a third moment

00:05:18.824 --> 00:05:21.940
you can feel truly grateful for.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.365
Step in it.

00:05:23.365 --> 00:05:25.532
See it, feel it, be there.

00:05:27.373 --> 00:05:28.206
Feel the gratitude.

00:05:28.206 --> 00:05:29.541
What were you so grateful for?

00:05:29.541 --> 00:05:31.708
What are you grateful for?

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:35.725
And then maybe throw one extra one in.

00:05:35.725 --> 00:05:37.757
Think of a coincidence,

00:05:37.757 --> 00:05:39.566
you know we all love
when life happens for us,

00:05:39.566 --> 00:05:40.757
not to us.

00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:42.566
We love coincidences 'cuz
we didn't do anything,

00:05:42.566 --> 00:05:44.443
something happened for us.

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:45.342
You were going to do one thing

00:05:45.342 --> 00:05:47.560
and you met somebody that you
developed a partnership with

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:50.969
or became a friend or a lover
or the love of your life.

00:05:50.969 --> 00:05:55.168
Or maybe a business opportunity
came from a coincidence.

00:05:55.168 --> 00:05:57.037
Or an insight came from a coincidence,

00:05:57.037 --> 00:05:58.447
that's been so valuable in your life,

00:05:58.447 --> 00:05:59.283
something you're grateful for.

00:05:59.283 --> 00:06:01.103
What's the coincidence
that led to something

00:06:01.103 --> 00:06:02.936
you're so grateful for?

00:06:02.936 --> 00:06:05.603
And feel the gratitude for that.

00:06:09.227 --> 00:06:11.967
And was it coincidence or were you guided?

00:06:11.967 --> 00:06:13.437
Hmm.

00:06:13.437 --> 00:06:15.354
Now as you breathe in your heart,

00:06:15.354 --> 00:06:16.758
you've been doing this
for about two minutes.

00:06:16.758 --> 00:06:18.705
Keep breathing, keep feeling it,

00:06:18.705 --> 00:06:20.825
feeling grateful.

00:06:20.825 --> 00:06:24.055
Let's use this state to
solve the problem state.

00:06:24.055 --> 00:06:25.432
So the easy way to do that is,

00:06:25.432 --> 00:06:26.732
is keep breathing in your heart

00:06:26.732 --> 00:06:28.995
stay out of your head, in your heart,

00:06:28.995 --> 00:06:31.041
and think of that situation
that's unfinished business,

00:06:31.041 --> 00:06:33.142
that's stressed you out in the past.

00:06:33.142 --> 00:06:35.254
But keep breathing in
this beautiful state,

00:06:35.254 --> 00:06:37.653
and ask yourself this question:

00:06:37.653 --> 00:06:40.976
ask yourself all I need to
focus on, in that situation,

00:06:40.976 --> 00:06:44.524
all I need to focus on, all
I need to remember is what?

00:06:44.524 --> 00:06:46.080
Your heart knows.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.881
All I need to focus on,
all I need to remember,

00:06:47.881 --> 00:06:51.195
all I need to do in
that situation, is what?

00:06:51.195 --> 00:06:53.528
Your heart knows the answer.

00:06:54.644 --> 00:06:58.966
All I need to focus on,
all I need to remember,

00:06:58.966 --> 00:07:00.633
all I need to do is?

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:04.175
And then your heart
probably knows the answer.

00:07:04.175 --> 00:07:05.408
I've done this a million times,

00:07:05.408 --> 00:07:08.624
not every one of you, but a
normal room I'd have people say,

00:07:08.624 --> 00:07:11.080
"Raise your hand if you got that answer."

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:13.299
98, 99% of people usually do,

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:15.120
even with this simple technique.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.355
- [Leo] Optimism can be
stoked up, like a fire.

00:07:18.355 --> 00:07:20.548
You know, you've got a campfire,
and it's kind of dying down,

00:07:20.548 --> 00:07:22.085
and then you can blow air on it,

00:07:22.085 --> 00:07:25.503
you can put some more kindling on it

00:07:25.503 --> 00:07:28.937
and then it'll spark up, and flare up.

00:07:28.937 --> 00:07:30.869
Well that's what you can
do with your optimism.

00:07:30.869 --> 00:07:32.884
So right now maybe you're
just kind of feeling at a

00:07:32.884 --> 00:07:34.357
at a baseline level,

00:07:34.357 --> 00:07:36.479
where you're not too
pessimistic about your future,

00:07:36.479 --> 00:07:38.888
but you're not too excited either.

00:07:38.888 --> 00:07:39.966
So what I recommend you do,

00:07:39.966 --> 00:07:41.392
is you do the following exercise.

00:07:41.392 --> 00:07:42.941
I want you to take your journal,

00:07:42.941 --> 00:07:44.871
piece of paper, something
where you can write,

00:07:44.871 --> 00:07:48.359
and I want you to write out and list,

00:07:48.359 --> 00:07:52.026
thirty things that
you're most excited about

00:07:53.892 --> 00:07:56.342
in the next year, that you're going to do.

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:59.551
Thirty things that you're
super super excited about.

00:07:59.551 --> 00:08:01.751
Maybe it's that vacation you want to take,

00:08:01.751 --> 00:08:04.829
maybe it's that relationship
that you hope to get into.

00:08:04.829 --> 00:08:07.631
Maybe it's that promotion at work
you know you're going to get.

00:08:07.631 --> 00:08:11.033
Maybe it's having all your
credit card debts eliminated.

00:08:11.033 --> 00:08:13.369
Maybe it's starting that
new business of yours,

00:08:13.369 --> 00:08:15.236
or starting that dream project

00:08:15.236 --> 00:08:17.282
or losing some weight.

00:08:17.282 --> 00:08:18.653
Whatever it is, but start writing it down

00:08:18.653 --> 00:08:20.506
and be as specific as possible.

00:08:20.506 --> 00:08:23.135
Thirty things that you're excited about

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:25.385
achieving in the next year,

00:08:26.317 --> 00:08:28.314
that really really motivate you.

00:08:28.314 --> 00:08:29.147
Try to focus on the ones
that get you excited.

00:08:29.147 --> 00:08:31.480
This is simple, this is all.

00:08:32.632 --> 00:08:34.196
This is the whole exercise.

00:08:34.196 --> 00:08:36.005
Sit down and actually do this,

00:08:36.005 --> 00:08:37.562
take 20 minutes or whatever it takes you

00:08:37.562 --> 00:08:39.429
to wite all this stuff out,

00:08:39.429 --> 00:08:41.255
and notice how you feel.

00:08:41.255 --> 00:08:43.036
Notice how you feel right now.

00:08:43.036 --> 00:08:45.288
Notice how you feel before
you do the exercise,

00:08:45.288 --> 00:08:46.846
and then I want you to notice how you feel

00:08:46.846 --> 00:08:49.181
after you finish it.

00:08:49.181 --> 00:08:50.659
If you're like me,

00:08:50.659 --> 00:08:53.958
you're going to feel so
much more optimistic.

00:08:53.958 --> 00:08:55.216
You're going to feel energized,

00:08:55.216 --> 00:08:56.710
you're going to feel happy,
you're going to feel alive.

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.592
You're going to feel like
there's something to your life.

00:08:58.592 --> 00:09:00.825
Because your future now is bright,

00:09:00.825 --> 00:09:02.323
and it's right here before your eyes.

00:09:02.323 --> 00:09:03.311
You've articulated it,

00:09:03.311 --> 00:09:05.032
you've layed it out very clearly,

00:09:05.032 --> 00:09:06.692
and it's right before you.

00:09:06.692 --> 00:09:09.783
I recommend you do this
exercise more than once.

00:09:09.783 --> 00:09:10.963
Do it right now

00:09:10.963 --> 00:09:13.747
but also continue to do
it throughout your life.

00:09:13.747 --> 00:09:16.407
Continue to do it, do it
at least once a month.

00:09:16.407 --> 00:09:19.224
Do it even once a week because

00:09:19.224 --> 00:09:20.702
it's going to get you connected back

00:09:20.702 --> 00:09:23.110
to the stuff that's exciting to you.

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:26.006
And it's also going to, you know
you're mind's going to brainstorm

00:09:26.006 --> 00:09:27.604
and come up with new
stuff to put on that list.

00:09:27.604 --> 00:09:28.437
And you can be brainstorming

00:09:28.437 --> 00:09:30.157
about what you're going to
be doing for the whole year,

00:09:30.157 --> 00:09:31.825
but you can also localize it down

00:09:31.825 --> 00:09:33.819
and you can shorten the timeframe

00:09:33.819 --> 00:09:35.529
to something like the next month,

00:09:35.529 --> 00:09:37.033
or even what you're going to be doing

00:09:37.033 --> 00:09:39.961
over the next week or even today.

00:09:39.961 --> 00:09:41.290
Even today you can do it.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:42.261
Just like what are five things

00:09:42.261 --> 00:09:43.748
you're going to be
excited about doing today?

00:09:43.748 --> 00:09:45.280
If you do that exercise in the morning,

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:46.610
just for five minutes,

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.271
what are the five things
you're going to be excited

00:09:48.271 --> 00:09:49.428
about doing today?

00:09:49.428 --> 00:09:51.701
It'll probably even take you
just two minutes to do that.

00:09:51.701 --> 00:09:53.347
You're going to feel you're
going to be much more excited

00:09:53.347 --> 00:09:54.312
about your day,

00:09:54.312 --> 00:09:56.591
and you're going to be
much more optimistic.

00:09:56.591 --> 00:09:57.606
- [Michael] I was going through some stuff

00:09:57.606 --> 00:09:59.603
and a woman said this to me, she was like,

00:09:59.603 --> 00:10:01.633
"When you walk through a
doorway, say an affirmation."

00:10:01.633 --> 00:10:03.076
And if you think about it,

00:10:03.076 --> 00:10:05.246
think about how many doorways
you walk through in a day.

00:10:05.246 --> 00:10:08.184
A bathroom door, your bedroom door,

00:10:08.184 --> 00:10:09.784
a door of a building.

00:10:09.784 --> 00:10:11.279
Your office door, in, out.

00:10:11.279 --> 00:10:13.107
Every time you go in or out of a door,

00:10:13.107 --> 00:10:15.085
you have to say something
positive about yourself.

00:10:15.085 --> 00:10:16.264
Or something that you believe.

00:10:16.264 --> 00:10:18.270
It's insane if you try it,

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:22.129
'cuz you end up saying like
400 things or 500 things a day.

00:10:22.129 --> 00:10:25.946
And it's pretty incredible
how fast you see

00:10:25.946 --> 00:10:29.113
the things that you say inside of you.

00:10:30.402 --> 00:10:32.556
And that was something that
was really powerful for me.

00:10:32.556 --> 00:10:33.942
- [Brian] I want to talk to you now

00:10:33.942 --> 00:10:37.059
about the big difference
between optimists and pessimists

00:10:37.059 --> 00:10:37.892
in life.

00:10:37.892 --> 00:10:40.591
Between happy, excited, fulfilled people

00:10:40.591 --> 00:10:43.616
and negative, tiring, depressed people.

00:10:43.616 --> 00:10:46.375
Now everyone wants to
be physically healthy,

00:10:46.375 --> 00:10:49.692
but it's important to want to
be mentally healthy as well.

00:10:49.692 --> 00:10:53.933
The true measure of mental
fitness is how optimistic you are

00:10:53.933 --> 00:10:56.350
about yourself and your life.

00:10:57.361 --> 00:10:59.794
Now in order to become truly optimistic,

00:10:59.794 --> 00:11:02.437
you must learn how to
control your thinking

00:11:02.437 --> 00:11:04.216
in very specific ways,

00:11:04.216 --> 00:11:08.088
so that you feel terrific about
yourself in your situation,

00:11:08.088 --> 00:11:11.505
most of the time, no matter what happens.

00:11:12.911 --> 00:11:15.450
There are three basic
differences in the reactions

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:17.714
of optimists and pessimists.

00:11:17.714 --> 00:11:19.275
The first difference is that

00:11:19.275 --> 00:11:22.252
the optimist sees a set back as temporary,

00:11:22.252 --> 00:11:25.794
while the pessimist sees it as permanent.

00:11:25.794 --> 00:11:28.203
The optimist sees an unfortunate event,

00:11:28.203 --> 00:11:30.477
such as an order that falls through,

00:11:30.477 --> 00:11:33.721
or a sales call that fails,
as a temporary event,

00:11:33.721 --> 00:11:35.697
something that is limited in time

00:11:35.697 --> 00:11:38.267
and that has no real impact on the future.

00:11:38.267 --> 00:11:40.148
The pessimist on the other hand,

00:11:40.148 --> 00:11:42.623
sees negative events as permanent,

00:11:42.623 --> 00:11:44.963
as part of life and destiny.

00:11:44.963 --> 00:11:47.553
The optimist makes a
mistake and brushes it off.

00:11:47.553 --> 00:11:48.978
The pessimist makes a mistake

00:11:48.978 --> 00:11:52.273
and considers that he or she
is not really good enough.

00:11:52.273 --> 00:11:53.839
He or she is not competent,

00:11:53.839 --> 00:11:56.811
he or she is not likable,
popular, or successful,

00:11:56.811 --> 00:12:00.978
and becomes depressed,
becomes crizest by self pity,

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:06.518
sees themself as a victim,
and feels like quitting.

00:12:06.518 --> 00:12:09.314
The second difference between
the optimist and the pessimist

00:12:09.314 --> 00:12:12.959
is that the optimist sees
difficulties as specific,

00:12:12.959 --> 00:12:16.472
while the pessimist
sees them as pervasive.

00:12:16.472 --> 00:12:17.936
This is really important.

00:12:17.936 --> 00:12:20.720
This means that when things
go wrong for the optimist,

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:23.485
he looks as the event
as an isolated incident,

00:12:23.485 --> 00:12:25.983
largely disconnected from other things

00:12:25.983 --> 00:12:27.624
that are going on in his life.

00:12:27.624 --> 00:12:30.786
He deals with it and gets
busy, and puts it behind him.

00:12:30.786 --> 00:12:33.063
For example, if something
you were counting on

00:12:33.063 --> 00:12:36.434
failed to materialize, and
you interpret it to yourself

00:12:36.434 --> 00:12:38.519
as being an unfortunate event,

00:12:38.519 --> 00:12:41.191
but something that happens
in the course of life

00:12:41.191 --> 00:12:44.310
and business, you know, stuff happens,

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:47.423
you would be reacting like an optimist.

00:12:47.423 --> 00:12:49.278
The pessimist on the
other hand, is different.

00:12:49.278 --> 00:12:52.974
The pessimist sees disappointments
as being pervasive,

00:12:52.974 --> 00:12:54.917
"Oh, whoa me."

00:12:54.917 --> 00:12:57.658
To him, those setbacks are indications

00:12:57.658 --> 00:12:59.661
of a problem or shortcomings

00:12:59.661 --> 00:13:02.657
that pervades every
area of his or her life.

00:13:02.657 --> 00:13:06.948
They have this, "What's
the use?" attitude.

00:13:06.948 --> 00:13:10.195
The third difference between
the optimist and pessimist

00:13:10.195 --> 00:13:12.872
is that optimists see events as external,

00:13:12.872 --> 00:13:16.433
while pessimists interpret
events as personal.

00:13:16.433 --> 00:13:18.876
When things go wrong, the
optimist will stand to see

00:13:18.876 --> 00:13:22.278
that set back is resulting
from external factors

00:13:22.278 --> 00:13:25.111
over which one has little control.

00:13:26.462 --> 00:13:29.245
For example, if the optimist
is cut off in traffic,

00:13:29.245 --> 00:13:31.449
instead of getting angry or upset,

00:13:31.449 --> 00:13:34.424
he will simply downgrade
the importance of the event

00:13:34.424 --> 00:13:36.559
by saying something like, "Oh well,

00:13:36.559 --> 00:13:38.552
I guess that person's
just having a bad day.

00:13:38.552 --> 00:13:41.619
Or maybe he or she is in
a hurry to get to work.

00:13:41.619 --> 00:13:43.183
Or something like that."

00:13:43.183 --> 00:13:44.603
The pessimist on the other hand,

00:13:44.603 --> 00:13:48.714
has a tendency to take
everything personally.

00:13:48.714 --> 00:13:50.762
If the pessimist is cut off in traffic,

00:13:50.762 --> 00:13:54.165
he or she will react as
though the other driver

00:13:54.165 --> 00:13:56.107
has gotten up that morning,

00:13:56.107 --> 00:13:59.424
and driven through traffic
and deliberately acted

00:13:59.424 --> 00:14:03.093
to cut him off, to make
him upset and angry.

00:14:03.093 --> 00:14:05.148
The hallmark of the fully mature,

00:14:05.148 --> 00:14:08.384
fully functioning, self
actualizing personality,

00:14:08.384 --> 00:14:11.897
is the ability to be
objective and unemotional

00:14:11.897 --> 00:14:16.064
when caught up in the
inevitable storms of daily life.

00:14:17.722 --> 00:14:20.104
The superior person has the ability to

00:14:20.104 --> 00:14:22.881
continue talking to himself in a positive

00:14:22.881 --> 00:14:24.082
and optimistic way,

00:14:24.082 --> 00:14:26.424
keeping his mind calm and clear

00:14:26.424 --> 00:14:29.485
and completely under control.

00:14:29.485 --> 00:14:32.639
The mature personality is
more relaxed and aware,

00:14:32.639 --> 00:14:36.693
and capable of interpreting
events more realistically

00:14:36.693 --> 00:14:40.860
and less emotionally than
is the immature personality.

00:14:42.138 --> 00:14:46.178
As a result, the mature person
exerts a far greater sense

00:14:46.178 --> 00:14:49.871
of control and influence
over his environment

00:14:49.871 --> 00:14:54.038
and is far less likely to be
angry or upset or distracted.

00:14:55.157 --> 00:14:57.168
As the Buddhists say, "The immature person

00:14:57.168 --> 00:14:59.331
practices detachment.

00:14:59.331 --> 00:15:01.150
And though they're concerned about things,

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:04.900
they don't get excited,
they just stay calm."

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:09.145
Starting today, resolve
to think like an optimist,

00:15:09.145 --> 00:15:10.736
no matter what happens.

00:15:10.736 --> 00:15:12.860
Look for the good in every situation.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:14.772
Look for a lesson that you can learn

00:15:14.772 --> 00:15:17.490
when you have a failure or a set back.

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:19.980
You may not be able to control events,

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:22.873
but you can control the
way you react to them,

00:15:22.873 --> 00:15:26.223
and in doing that, you
control your whole life.

00:15:26.223 --> 00:15:29.078
- [Robin] How do you really take a bad day

00:15:29.078 --> 00:15:31.117
and restructure it,

00:15:31.117 --> 00:15:33.814
so that you can actually turn
it into something valuable?

00:15:33.814 --> 00:15:35.585
And so I'm going to share with you,

00:15:35.585 --> 00:15:38.335
the five P's of turning a bad day

00:15:39.282 --> 00:15:42.520
into a valuable day, and even an epic day.

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:44.069
And I'm going to dial
right into the first one,

00:15:44.069 --> 00:15:45.770
which is Perspective.

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:49.160
Perspective is a word
that seems very simple

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:51.173
but I think it's very powerful.

00:15:51.173 --> 00:15:52.923
It's very easy to get

00:15:53.945 --> 00:15:56.902
seduced into making something small,

00:15:56.902 --> 00:15:59.477
a lot larger than it is.

00:15:59.477 --> 00:16:01.841
And perspective simply reminds us

00:16:01.841 --> 00:16:04.890
to go to 50,000 feet on a bad day,

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.836
and count our blessings.

00:16:06.836 --> 00:16:08.724
Perspective simply reminds us

00:16:08.724 --> 00:16:11.474
that things could be a lot worse.

00:16:12.609 --> 00:16:16.113
Perspective on a bad day,
is simply understanding

00:16:16.113 --> 00:16:19.719
that we live in a world where
half the world's population

00:16:19.719 --> 00:16:22.302
lives on less than $2.50 a day.

00:16:24.622 --> 00:16:27.216
Perspective on a bad day,
is reminding yourself

00:16:27.216 --> 00:16:29.541
of that Persian proverb, of which says,

00:16:29.541 --> 00:16:31.951
"I curse the fact I had no shoes,

00:16:31.951 --> 00:16:34.996
until I saw the man who had no feet."

00:16:34.996 --> 00:16:38.524
Perspective is such a powerful word.

00:16:38.524 --> 00:16:41.456
Here's a great question on a bad day,

00:16:41.456 --> 00:16:43.901
to bring on some perspective.

00:16:43.901 --> 00:16:46.025
Has anyone died here?

00:16:46.025 --> 00:16:47.543
So perspective is something

00:16:47.543 --> 00:16:49.930
I really want you to think
about, and on a bad day,

00:16:49.930 --> 00:16:53.891
it will actually allow you
to turn the lead into gold

00:16:53.891 --> 00:16:55.211
and really pivot.

00:16:55.211 --> 00:16:58.017
Which brings me to the second P,

00:16:58.017 --> 00:17:00.722
of turning a bad day, into a great day,

00:17:00.722 --> 00:17:02.094
and it's Pivot.

00:17:02.094 --> 00:17:05.375
And here's the question
to really help you pivot.

00:17:05.375 --> 00:17:08.458
W T O H: What's The Opportunity Here?

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:11.221
So you're having a bad day,

00:17:11.221 --> 00:17:12.839
maybe you had a fight with someone,

00:17:12.839 --> 00:17:15.313
maybe you lost a big sale,

00:17:15.313 --> 00:17:17.791
maybe someone cut you off in traffic,

00:17:17.791 --> 00:17:20.972
and then you didn't get
your favorite lunch,

00:17:20.972 --> 00:17:24.063
and then you missed getting
into Soul Cycle Class.

00:17:24.063 --> 00:17:26.650
And then you had a
difficulty on the way home,

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.841
so let's say that's happening.

00:17:28.841 --> 00:17:32.574
You simply run the W T O H question,

00:17:32.574 --> 00:17:34.328
which will allow you to pivot.

00:17:34.328 --> 00:17:37.856
W T O H: What's The Opportunity Here?

00:17:37.856 --> 00:17:40.380
See there's great power in a question.

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:44.717
And it allows your brain
to hunt for something good.

00:17:44.717 --> 00:17:46.514
And so how do you pivot?

00:17:46.514 --> 00:17:49.507
You ask yourself: What's
The Opportunity Here?

00:17:49.507 --> 00:17:51.009
You have a fight with someone,

00:17:51.009 --> 00:17:53.559
let's say one of your family members,

00:17:53.559 --> 00:17:56.048
you say, "What's the opportunity here?"

00:17:56.048 --> 00:17:59.095
Well, your brain then starts
to look for the opportunity,

00:17:59.095 --> 00:18:02.106
which is, I can learn how
to communicate better.

00:18:02.106 --> 00:18:04.820
Or this is an opportunity
for me to show forgiveness

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:06.977
and grow in my personal bravery.

00:18:06.977 --> 00:18:09.543
This is an opportunity
for me to understand

00:18:09.543 --> 00:18:11.440
my family member better.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:13.988
It's a great and powerful question.

00:18:13.988 --> 00:18:16.621
Which brings me to my third P,

00:18:16.621 --> 00:18:19.831
in turning a bad day into a great day,

00:18:19.831 --> 00:18:22.336
and it's really Pharmacy.

00:18:22.336 --> 00:18:24.184
The third P is Pharmacy,

00:18:24.184 --> 00:18:25.905
and that's all about moving.

00:18:25.905 --> 00:18:27.285
When I have a difficult day,

00:18:27.285 --> 00:18:28.673
here's one of the first things I do,

00:18:28.673 --> 00:18:30.386
I will get on my mountain bike

00:18:30.386 --> 00:18:34.688
and I will ride like
a bat out of wherever,

00:18:34.688 --> 00:18:39.174
through the forest, and that
releases dopamine in my brain,

00:18:39.174 --> 00:18:42.512
which is the neurotransmitter
of inspiration.

00:18:42.512 --> 00:18:44.578
And that releases serotonin, moving,

00:18:44.578 --> 00:18:47.375
ride on the bicycle,
it releases serotonin,

00:18:47.375 --> 00:18:50.499
which is the pleasure neurotransmitter.

00:18:50.499 --> 00:18:52.449
And it cuts down on my cortisol,

00:18:52.449 --> 00:18:54.543
which is the fear hormone.

00:18:54.543 --> 00:18:57.786
So just simply going for
a mountain bike ride,

00:18:57.786 --> 00:18:58.939
or going for a swim,

00:18:58.939 --> 00:19:00.854
or getting into yoga class,

00:19:00.854 --> 00:19:02.862
or something as simple
as going for a walk,

00:19:02.862 --> 00:19:07.184
or maybe even doing jumping
jacks when no one's looking,

00:19:07.184 --> 00:19:11.288
will create a pharmacy of
mastery within your brain,

00:19:11.288 --> 00:19:13.445
which will affect your psychology,

00:19:13.445 --> 00:19:16.702
your neurobiology, and your interior life,

00:19:16.702 --> 00:19:18.329
which makes you feel just a lot better.

00:19:18.329 --> 00:19:19.162
You know that.

00:19:19.162 --> 00:19:22.106
After a workout, you always
feel different than you did

00:19:22.106 --> 00:19:23.721
before you went into the workout.

00:19:23.721 --> 00:19:25.806
And related to the pharmacy of mastery,

00:19:25.806 --> 00:19:29.393
is something that I have
counted on for years,

00:19:29.393 --> 00:19:30.976
when I've had good seasons,

00:19:30.976 --> 00:19:33.394
when I've had challenging
seasons of my life,

00:19:33.394 --> 00:19:34.616
massage.

00:19:34.616 --> 00:19:36.623
I call it the two massage protocol:

00:19:36.623 --> 00:19:39.335
two massages every single week,

00:19:39.335 --> 00:19:42.379
it moves your lymph, it moves your blood,

00:19:42.379 --> 00:19:44.228
which oxygenates your system,

00:19:44.228 --> 00:19:47.737
it reduces toxicity, you
feel a whole lot better.

00:19:47.737 --> 00:19:50.425
Which brings me to the fourth P,

00:19:50.425 --> 00:19:54.912
in turning a bad day
into a great day: Pages.

00:19:54.912 --> 00:19:56.576
You know I love journaling,

00:19:56.576 --> 00:19:59.843
and for hundreds and hundreds of years,

00:19:59.843 --> 00:20:02.525
people who have gone through difficulty,

00:20:02.525 --> 00:20:06.435
people who are experiencing
calamity and chaos,

00:20:06.435 --> 00:20:07.602
open a journal

00:20:08.932 --> 00:20:11.603
turn to a fresh white page,

00:20:11.603 --> 00:20:14.904
and pour their pain or
pour their confusion,

00:20:14.904 --> 00:20:18.290
pour their frustration,
out onto that page.

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:20.688
It does something so powerful.

00:20:20.688 --> 00:20:23.116
It allows for a profound release

00:20:23.116 --> 00:20:26.140
of what you're experiencing,
out onto the written page.

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:28.350
Here's the key, if you will repress

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:30.293
and suppress your feelings,

00:20:30.293 --> 00:20:33.960
of anger, of sadness, of disappointment,

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:37.145
all of those lower energy feelings,

00:20:37.145 --> 00:20:39.145
if you keep them inside,

00:20:40.025 --> 00:20:42.989
they not only build up toxicity,

00:20:42.989 --> 00:20:46.343
and they build up
resentment and frustration,

00:20:46.343 --> 00:20:49.565
but those are the very things
that lead to inflammation,

00:20:49.565 --> 00:20:51.315
that create dis-ease.

00:20:52.208 --> 00:20:53.565
And so what I'm sharing with you,

00:20:53.565 --> 00:20:56.638
with great love and respect,
is really very potent.

00:20:56.638 --> 00:20:59.596
Pages, the fourth four
of turning a bad day

00:20:59.596 --> 00:21:00.700
into a great day.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:03.964
Pull out your journal and
write what you're feeling

00:21:03.964 --> 00:21:06.797
onto a fresh, crisp, written page.

00:21:08.056 --> 00:21:10.838
Which brings me to my fifth and final P,

00:21:10.838 --> 00:21:14.233
in the five P's of turning
a bad day into a great day,

00:21:14.233 --> 00:21:15.965
the Planet.

00:21:15.965 --> 00:21:17.808
Now you're saying, "Robin, what
are you talking about here?"

00:21:17.808 --> 00:21:19.167
Well, nature.

00:21:19.167 --> 00:21:22.417
Nature is life's sweet recovery method.

00:21:24.616 --> 00:21:27.312
Going for a walk in the woods,

00:21:27.312 --> 00:21:31.397
or walking on a beach and
getting next to the ocean,

00:21:31.397 --> 00:21:33.777
or if you live near a
desert, getting out there.

00:21:33.777 --> 00:21:36.011
If you're blessed to
live by the mountains,

00:21:36.011 --> 00:21:37.818
you know what I'm talking about.

00:21:37.818 --> 00:21:42.382
But when you go out to
nature, it grounds you.

00:21:42.382 --> 00:21:45.137
When you connect with
the planet, again nature,

00:21:45.137 --> 00:21:46.177
what does it do?

00:21:46.177 --> 00:21:49.562
It gives you that recovery method

00:21:49.562 --> 00:21:51.867
so you actually breathe in the fresh air,

00:21:51.867 --> 00:21:52.983
but it reminds you,

00:21:52.983 --> 00:21:56.614
you are part of something so
much bigger than yourself.

00:21:56.614 --> 00:21:58.531
And maybe your bad day,

00:22:00.965 --> 00:22:03.065
is taking you to a better place.

00:22:03.065 --> 00:22:04.467
You know, you've heard that old idea,

00:22:04.467 --> 00:22:07.552
but life doesn't really happen to you,

00:22:07.552 --> 00:22:10.613
life really happens for you.

00:22:10.613 --> 00:22:13.614
And there is this incredible
intelligence to life,

00:22:13.614 --> 00:22:15.093
we don't understand it.

00:22:15.093 --> 00:22:18.208
Look, you and I are humans, we resist it.

00:22:18.208 --> 00:22:20.908
But what if the thing you see as bad,

00:22:20.908 --> 00:22:25.075
is just your false belief
system, judging it as bad.

00:22:26.081 --> 00:22:27.030
We all know this.

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:30.250
The things that we see as bad,

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:33.484
over time, turned out to be blessings.

00:22:33.484 --> 00:22:35.799
And so everything is
really happening for you,

00:22:35.799 --> 00:22:37.034
for your best interests.

00:22:37.034 --> 00:22:38.961
It's taking you to a better place,

00:22:38.961 --> 00:22:40.588
it's making you stronger,

00:22:40.588 --> 00:22:43.984
it's teaching you great
lessons, often we resist it,

00:22:43.984 --> 00:22:45.615
but it all comes for our good.

00:22:45.615 --> 00:22:48.794
So those are the five
P's to take a bad day

00:22:48.794 --> 00:22:52.667
and really transmute it into a great day.

00:22:52.667 --> 00:22:55.246
Definitely do these five,

00:22:55.246 --> 00:22:56.668
because these are all muscles,

00:22:56.668 --> 00:22:59.286
and like anything, the more you practice,

00:22:59.286 --> 00:23:02.766
the stronger and more
fluent you're going to get.

00:23:02.766 --> 00:23:04.646
And if you keep on practicing,

00:23:04.646 --> 00:23:07.979
you are going to get to a place
where everyone else is feeling,

00:23:07.979 --> 00:23:11.134
"Oh, I've gone through this
difficulty, it's a bad day,"

00:23:11.134 --> 00:23:13.164
and you're going to see it as possibility

00:23:13.164 --> 00:23:16.994
and you're going to be masterful
at turning the difficulty

00:23:16.994 --> 00:23:18.228
into opportunity.

00:23:18.228 --> 00:23:19.173
Hope I've been of service,

00:23:19.173 --> 00:23:21.006
I'll talk to you soon.

00:23:22.935 --> 00:23:24.207
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:23:24.207 --> 00:23:25.990
I'd love to know, what did you think?

00:23:25.990 --> 00:23:27.370
What did you learn from this video,

00:23:27.370 --> 00:23:29.650
that you're going to
apply immediately somehow

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:31.437
to your life or to your business?

