Better than anyone.

00:24:57.080 --> 00:24:59.934
- And now, you might
also have this objection

00:24:59.934 --> 00:25:03.010
over this thought, that
goes something like this,

00:25:03.010 --> 00:25:05.292
"Well, Leo, okay positive thinking.

00:25:05.292 --> 00:25:07.438
I hear you, it sounds nice.

00:25:07.438 --> 00:25:11.111
But isn't positive thinking
actually dangerous?

00:25:11.111 --> 00:25:12.592
I mean, I'm a realist.

00:25:12.592 --> 00:25:15.299
Isn't it better to be a realist in life?

00:25:15.299 --> 00:25:18.819
Rather than to be this
starry eyed optimist?

00:25:18.819 --> 00:25:20.400
And approach everything optimistically?

00:25:20.400 --> 00:25:21.934
Isn't realism the best approach?

00:25:21.934 --> 00:25:23.087
I mean, what if you're optimistic

00:25:23.087 --> 00:25:25.485
and then you're all about optimism,

00:25:25.485 --> 00:25:26.895
that you have all those goals and dreams

00:25:26.895 --> 00:25:28.588
and the outcomes that
you set for yourself,

00:25:28.588 --> 00:25:30.722
all those just come crashing down when it

00:25:30.722 --> 00:25:33.075
comes and kind of collides with reality?

00:25:33.075 --> 00:25:35.211
What if you're cheerful
and you're telling yourself

00:25:35.211 --> 00:25:36.896
to be all happy, and then
someone close to you dies,

00:25:36.896 --> 00:25:38.735
and then you're not able to maintain that?

00:25:38.735 --> 00:25:39.771
What happens then Leo?

00:25:39.771 --> 00:25:41.452
Isn't that reckless? Isn't that dangerous?

00:25:41.452 --> 00:25:44.139
Aren't you setting yourself up for pain?"

00:25:44.139 --> 00:25:46.740
And the answer is this:

00:25:46.740 --> 00:25:49.151
you are setting yourself up for pain,

00:25:49.151 --> 00:25:49.984
if what you're doing is

00:25:49.984 --> 00:25:52.701
you're setting these hard expectations,

00:25:52.701 --> 00:25:55.896
and you're very attached to the outcome.

00:25:55.896 --> 00:25:57.665
But it doesn't have to be that way.

00:25:57.665 --> 00:25:59.621
Right? See, this where discounters

00:25:59.621 --> 00:26:01.687
and naysayers of positive thinking,

00:26:01.687 --> 00:26:02.936
will get it wrong.

00:26:02.936 --> 00:26:04.174
Is they'll say, "Well positive thinking,

00:26:04.174 --> 00:26:07.028
that's going to set me up for failure.

00:26:07.028 --> 00:26:09.041
That's going to set up to disappointment."

00:26:09.041 --> 00:26:10.779
The problem is, they're being positive,

00:26:10.779 --> 00:26:12.602
and they're telling their
self, "Well, I'm positive,

00:26:12.602 --> 00:26:14.431
and I need the outcome to be positive.

00:26:14.431 --> 00:26:17.989
And if it's not positive, then
everything's going to Hell."

00:26:17.989 --> 00:26:20.119
But see, true positive thinking is like

00:26:20.119 --> 00:26:21.641
be more relaxed, be more chill,

00:26:21.641 --> 00:26:23.591
be outcome detached.

00:26:23.591 --> 00:26:24.941
You're a positive thinker,

00:26:24.941 --> 00:26:26.840
you're thinking positive
about the situation,

00:26:26.840 --> 00:26:29.843
that doesn't mean that the
situation won't turn bad.

00:26:29.843 --> 00:26:31.777
That doesn't mean that you
can foretell the future

00:26:31.777 --> 00:26:33.033
and you can get everything that you want

00:26:33.033 --> 00:26:34.164
to happen in your life,

00:26:34.164 --> 00:26:36.248
to happen in the way that you want it;

00:26:36.248 --> 00:26:37.887
never going to happen.

00:26:37.887 --> 00:26:39.793
On the contrary, it means
that you're going to have

00:26:39.793 --> 00:26:42.401
ups and downs, you're going to
have things unexpectedly happen.

00:26:42.401 --> 00:26:44.033
You might have some sort of lofty ambition

00:26:44.033 --> 00:26:45.263
or goal for your business,

00:26:45.263 --> 00:26:46.625
and then it comes crashing down,

00:26:46.625 --> 00:26:49.958
and it, you know, the
market comes and it crashes,

00:26:49.958 --> 00:26:51.729
and your business crashes with it.

00:26:51.729 --> 00:26:53.587
Or maybe you have some nice expectations

00:26:53.587 --> 00:26:56.489
and you're thinking very
positive about your relationship

00:26:56.489 --> 00:26:59.453
and then your relationship
ends in a divorce.

00:26:59.453 --> 00:27:01.398
That could happen.

00:27:01.398 --> 00:27:03.746
So I'm not saying you can
necessarily prevent that

00:27:03.746 --> 00:27:05.092
in all situations.

00:27:05.092 --> 00:27:07.394
But the idea here is that,
if you're a positive thinker,

00:27:07.394 --> 00:27:10.719
you remain positive, and
you're not attached to it.

00:27:10.719 --> 00:27:13.150
See if you're a realist or a pessimist,

00:27:13.150 --> 00:27:14.568
then actually what you're
doing is you're like,

00:27:14.568 --> 00:27:16.302
"Okay, if I'm thinking positive,

00:27:16.302 --> 00:27:18.281
then I need it to actually pan out.

00:27:18.281 --> 00:27:20.701
I need it to be positive all the time."

00:27:20.701 --> 00:27:22.298
And of course that's not going to work.

00:27:22.298 --> 00:27:24.838
That's a neurotic way of
doing positive thinking.

00:27:24.838 --> 00:27:26.448
True positive thinking is
like being cool and chill

00:27:26.448 --> 00:27:28.087
and is like, "You know
what, if it happens, good.

00:27:28.087 --> 00:27:32.193
And if it doesn't happen,
you know, still good."

00:27:32.193 --> 00:27:34.751
Heads I win, tails I win,

00:27:34.751 --> 00:27:38.122
that's what a true
positive attitude is about.

00:27:38.122 --> 00:27:39.973
Alright so, I'm going to wrap it up here.

00:27:39.973 --> 00:27:42.614
This is what cultivating
a positive attitude means.

00:27:42.614 --> 00:27:44.846
It's really about acceptance.

00:27:44.846 --> 00:27:46.282
You have to accept.

00:27:46.282 --> 00:27:47.458
What do you have to accept?

00:27:47.458 --> 00:27:49.348
One: you have to accept
the present moment,

00:27:49.348 --> 00:27:51.597
as it is, completely inevitable.

00:27:51.597 --> 00:27:53.670
Number two: you have to accept that worry

00:27:53.670 --> 00:27:56.481
is completely useless
and of no value to you.

00:27:56.481 --> 00:27:58.731
Number three: you have to
accept that cheerfulness

00:27:58.731 --> 00:28:02.481
is the best strategy to
go through life with.

00:28:03.623 --> 00:28:06.618
And you have to now
strive to live up to that.

00:28:06.618 --> 00:28:07.902
Right, I know it's hard,

00:28:07.902 --> 00:28:09.132
this doesn't mean it's easy,

00:28:09.132 --> 00:28:10.490
It's going to be very hard.

00:28:10.490 --> 00:28:11.931
But, if you're like me,

00:28:11.931 --> 00:28:15.195
then you see the longterm potential here.

00:28:15.195 --> 00:28:16.504
I mean, how awesome would it be

00:28:16.504 --> 00:28:18.595
to develop yourself internally?

00:28:18.595 --> 00:28:22.628
So that you could have a true
positive attitude about life?

00:28:22.628 --> 00:28:23.814
So that no matter what happens to you,

00:28:23.814 --> 00:28:25.220
you can remain cheerful,

00:28:25.220 --> 00:28:26.405
so that you're not worrying,

00:28:26.405 --> 00:28:28.318
and you're not feeling
like you have to worry

00:28:28.318 --> 00:28:30.464
because you know that the
worry is not helping you.

00:28:30.464 --> 00:28:32.198
And that you're in the present moment

00:28:32.198 --> 00:28:34.181
and you accept the moment as it is.

00:28:34.181 --> 00:28:35.685
If you can achieve all those things,

00:28:35.685 --> 00:28:38.086
then you've basically
accomplished nirvana;

00:28:38.086 --> 00:28:40.022
you've got Heaven on Earth,

00:28:40.022 --> 00:28:43.118
like nothing can hurt
you, you're untouchable.

00:28:43.118 --> 00:28:45.684
So this is a very powerful
goal to set for yourself,

00:28:45.684 --> 00:28:49.263
is to cultivate this attitude
over the months and the years,

00:28:49.263 --> 00:28:51.376
as you're growing yourself
and you're doing other stuff,

00:28:51.376 --> 00:28:53.815
try to move you way and inch your way up,

00:28:53.815 --> 00:28:57.237
to having a true positive
attitude about life.

00:28:57.237 --> 00:29:00.207
- [Wengie] One thing that I've found,

00:29:00.207 --> 00:29:02.698
like really really hard about optimism,

00:29:02.698 --> 00:29:04.410
is that you can't expect to become

00:29:04.410 --> 00:29:07.852
an optimistic person
overnight, it does not happen.

00:29:07.852 --> 00:29:10.722
It's probably taken me like five years

00:29:10.722 --> 00:29:14.350
of constant practicing to
become an optimistic person,

00:29:14.350 --> 00:29:17.203
or someone that can see
the bright side of things.

00:29:17.203 --> 00:29:19.260
And when I'm in a bad mood or something,

00:29:19.260 --> 00:29:21.534
I tend to go back to my old habits

00:29:21.534 --> 00:29:23.589
and think really negatively.

00:29:23.589 --> 00:29:27.366
But in general, it gets
easier and easier to,

00:29:27.366 --> 00:29:30.103
I guess, have a better
perspective on things,

00:29:30.103 --> 00:29:31.354
as you practice.

00:29:31.354 --> 00:29:34.465
So for those of you guys
wondering why it's so hard

00:29:34.465 --> 00:29:38.502
to be optimistic, don't need to wonder,

00:29:38.502 --> 00:29:40.029
it is really really hard,

00:29:40.029 --> 00:29:42.086
especially if it doesn't come naturally,

00:29:42.086 --> 00:29:45.546
but I know that you can be an
optimistic person if you try.

00:29:45.546 --> 00:29:47.188
So I'm going to be showing some of my tips

00:29:47.188 --> 00:29:49.521
that I have used to help me.

00:29:50.708 --> 00:29:53.683
And I believe everyone is born with

00:29:53.683 --> 00:29:56.044
sort of a natural level of happiness,

00:29:56.044 --> 00:29:58.799
and there have been
scientific research studies

00:29:58.799 --> 00:30:00.095
that have been done,

00:30:00.095 --> 00:30:03.072
that everyone comes with
a baseline of happiness.

00:30:03.072 --> 00:30:05.246
And whatever that is for you,

00:30:05.246 --> 00:30:08.516
that is kind of where
you naturally will sit.

00:30:08.516 --> 00:30:12.382
So if you're born like someone
that isn't naturally happy,

00:30:12.382 --> 00:30:14.187
you have a lot more work to do,

00:30:14.187 --> 00:30:16.564
and you need a little bit more practice

00:30:16.564 --> 00:30:18.577
but there's nothing wrong with you.

00:30:18.577 --> 00:30:21.775
And if you're born a super happy person,

00:30:21.775 --> 00:30:24.244
then you don't really
need to try very hard

00:30:24.244 --> 00:30:25.279
to be optimistic.

00:30:25.279 --> 00:30:28.077
And if you are born
someone that, you know,

00:30:28.077 --> 00:30:31.336
wasn't born super duper like
happy go lucky kind of person,

00:30:31.336 --> 00:30:33.919
you may look around and see these people

00:30:33.919 --> 00:30:35.788
always being so cheerful and bubbly,

00:30:35.788 --> 00:30:37.653
and wonder, how the Hell did they do it?

00:30:37.653 --> 00:30:40.398
Well, I believe they may
have been born with it.

00:30:40.398 --> 00:30:44.774
But you know, I don't
know, it's just science.

00:30:44.774 --> 00:30:47.188
So, I guess for those of you
that have a baseline level

00:30:47.188 --> 00:30:48.771
that isn't as high,

00:30:48.771 --> 00:30:52.203
you just need to switch the
way you think about things.

00:30:52.203 --> 00:30:54.643
And I think this is
something I've been noticing

00:30:54.643 --> 00:30:57.586
really really like obviously lately.

00:30:57.586 --> 00:30:59.826
Like, with any given situation,

00:30:59.826 --> 00:31:02.877
there's always multiple
ways to look at it.

00:31:02.877 --> 00:31:05.326
Like if you get into a car accident,

00:31:05.326 --> 00:31:08.052
you can either feel like, you know,

00:31:08.052 --> 00:31:11.294
it's the worst thing that happened today.

00:31:11.294 --> 00:31:12.882
And you could also think,

00:31:12.882 --> 00:31:14.594
this is the luckiest day of my life

00:31:14.594 --> 00:31:17.729
because I'm still alive
after having a car accident.

00:31:17.729 --> 00:31:21.514
So a car accident can either
be super duper negative to you,

00:31:21.514 --> 00:31:24.335
or it can be like, oh my God, I'm alive.

00:31:24.335 --> 00:31:26.002
I better live my life better.

00:31:26.002 --> 00:31:28.423
So you can see how something
so tragic and terrible

00:31:28.423 --> 00:31:31.973
can have two sides of
the coin, pretty easily.

00:31:31.973 --> 00:31:34.460
Like I can imagine someone
feeling both feelings.

00:31:34.460 --> 00:31:38.236
And you'll probably know
someone in your life,

00:31:38.236 --> 00:31:41.418
that will experience
both of these feelings.

00:31:41.418 --> 00:31:44.896
So I guess when you look at
any situation objectively,

00:31:44.896 --> 00:31:46.542
it's kind of a choice.

00:31:46.542 --> 00:31:48.292
It's your choice to decide

00:31:48.292 --> 00:31:51.913
what any given situation means to you,

00:31:51.913 --> 00:31:53.750
and that is your decision to make,

00:31:53.750 --> 00:31:55.941
and no one else can force you to think

00:31:55.941 --> 00:31:57.279
like it's a negative situation,

00:31:57.279 --> 00:31:59.351
and no one else can force you

00:31:59.351 --> 00:32:01.245
to think it's a positive situation.

00:32:01.245 --> 00:32:03.123
I guess becoming an optimistic person

00:32:03.123 --> 00:32:05.269
means making that choice in your life,

00:32:05.269 --> 00:32:06.658
and then sticking to it,

00:32:06.658 --> 00:32:10.991
and being really aware of the
thoughts going in your head,

00:32:10.991 --> 00:32:12.860
and how you think, etc.

00:32:12.860 --> 00:32:14.858
Because someone can get cancer,

00:32:14.858 --> 00:32:17.662
and they can have two different reactions.

00:32:17.662 --> 00:32:19.857
One person may take it as

00:32:19.857 --> 00:32:24.469
it's their chance to do
everything that they wanted to do,

00:32:24.469 --> 00:32:25.685
and help people.

00:32:25.685 --> 00:32:27.584
And one may feel like a victim

00:32:27.584 --> 00:32:28.892
and think like it's the worst thing.

00:32:28.892 --> 00:32:30.313
Why did this happen to me?

00:32:30.313 --> 00:32:31.946
And then spend the rest of their days,

00:32:31.946 --> 00:32:34.978
mulling over and being really grumpy.

00:32:34.978 --> 00:32:36.963
It's your choice, really.

00:32:36.963 --> 00:32:40.438
And I know I'm using
really extreme examples,

00:32:40.438 --> 00:32:42.577
like accidents and cancer,

00:32:42.577 --> 00:32:45.811
but it's these extreme examples
that can really show you

00:32:45.811 --> 00:32:49.512
the glaring difference
between how people think.

00:32:49.512 --> 00:32:50.525
And even though

00:32:50.525 --> 00:32:53.489
you don't automatically
think optimistically,

00:32:53.489 --> 00:32:55.995
it doesn't mean you can't do it over time.

00:32:55.995 --> 00:32:58.824
So I always catch myself
doing things like this,

00:32:58.824 --> 00:33:01.047
if I catch myself thinking negative,

00:33:01.047 --> 00:33:03.153
I will stop, breathe,

00:33:03.153 --> 00:33:06.792
and then try and rethink
about the situation again.

00:33:06.792 --> 00:33:08.455
And then when you do that,

00:33:08.455 --> 00:33:12.704
that process becomes easier,
much like lifting weights.

00:33:12.704 --> 00:33:14.623
At first, lifting you know heavy weights,

00:33:14.623 --> 00:33:16.542
would be like really hard.

00:33:16.542 --> 00:33:18.720
But if you practice every single day

00:33:18.720 --> 00:33:21.670
and then just lift a little
bit more every single day,

00:33:21.670 --> 00:33:23.889
you will actually get really good at it.

00:33:23.889 --> 00:33:26.857
And I don't know why I always
use weights as an example,

00:33:26.857 --> 00:33:29.202
but I don't know, the gym is just my

00:33:29.202 --> 00:33:32.553
go to example for things,
I have no idea why.

00:33:32.553 --> 00:33:37.381
But yeah, so whatever
situation you're in right now,

00:33:37.381 --> 00:33:40.002
and you're feeling really down about it,

00:33:40.002 --> 00:33:42.755
I want you to sit down
with a piece of paper,

00:33:42.755 --> 00:33:43.930
or even in your mind,

00:33:43.930 --> 00:33:46.837
it really depends on which
way is easier for you,

00:33:46.837 --> 00:33:49.621
and to think of all the different ways

00:33:49.621 --> 00:33:52.419
someone can think of that situation.

00:33:52.419 --> 00:33:53.639
You don't have to put yourself

00:33:53.639 --> 00:33:55.865
in that situation personally yet.

00:33:55.865 --> 00:33:58.620
Pretend you have five different friends,

00:33:58.620 --> 00:34:01.832
how would each of them
think about this situation?

00:34:01.832 --> 00:34:03.829
And then you can list out all the ways

00:34:03.829 --> 00:34:05.787
I could think about it differently,

00:34:05.787 --> 00:34:07.345
and that will really open your eyes

00:34:07.345 --> 00:34:11.268
on the amount of ways that you
can think about it yourself.

00:34:11.268 --> 00:34:14.020
And then you can choose
the one that will help you

00:34:14.020 --> 00:34:14.920
the best.

00:34:14.920 --> 00:34:16.475
Because at the end of the day,

00:34:16.475 --> 00:34:18.037
whatever you think about the situation

00:34:18.037 --> 00:34:20.629
will determine what your future can be.

00:34:20.629 --> 00:34:25.172
Someone that thinks positively
of a really bad situation

00:34:25.172 --> 00:34:26.897
can end up being you know,

00:34:26.897 --> 00:34:29.118
the person that helps many other people

00:34:29.118 --> 00:34:31.557
in the same situation
through sharing their story,

00:34:31.557 --> 00:34:33.879
opening a charity, or
doing volunteer work.

00:34:33.879 --> 00:34:36.267
And then the other very same person

00:34:36.267 --> 00:34:38.925
can affect their future
by playing the victim

00:34:38.925 --> 00:34:40.834
and then spending the rest of their time

00:34:40.834 --> 00:34:42.352
making all their friends miserable

00:34:42.352 --> 00:34:45.602
by dragging them into their sad story.

